{"meta":{"id":"adria_series_ia_aeonfluxfullseries","type":"series","name":"Æon Flux Full Series","poster":"https://archive.org/services/img/aeonfluxfullseries","posterShape":"landscape","background":"https://archive.org/services/img/aeonfluxfullseries","description":"📦 Origem: Internet Archive (coleção aberta — confira a licença)\n\nÆon Flux /ˌiːɒn ˈflʌks/ is an American avant-garde science fiction adventure animated television series that aired on MTV from November 30, 1991, until October 10, 1995, with film, comic book, and video game adaptations following thereafter. It premiered on MTV's Liquid Television experimental animation show, as a six-part serial of short films, followed in 1992 by five individual short episodes. In 1995, a season of ten half-hour episodes aired as a stand-alone series. Æon Flux was created by American animator Peter Chung. Each Episode plots have elements of social science fiction, biopunk, allegory, dystopian fiction, spy fiction, psychological drama, postmodern visual, psychedelic imagery and Gnostic symbolism.\n\nPLOT:\n\nÆon Flux is set in a surreal German Expressionist style futuristic universe. The setting comprises a bizarre dystopia populated by mutant creatures, clones, and robots set within the two separated border wall cities of Monica and Bregna. The title character is a tall, sexy, dominatrix scantily-clad secret agent from the city of Monica, skilled in espionage, assassination and acrobatics. Her mission is to infiltrate and destroy the strongholds of the city of…","releaseInfo":"1991","year":"1991","genres":["Aeon flux","Æon flux","Mtv","Liquid television"],"links":[{"name":"Fonte original","category":"Origem","url":"https://archive.org/details/aeonfluxfullseries"}],"videos":[{"id":"adria_series_ia_aeonfluxfullseries_s1e1","title":"EP 1","season":1,"episode":1,"released":"1991-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","thumbnail":"https://archive.org/services/img/aeonfluxfullseries"},{"id":"adria_series_ia_aeonfluxfullseries_s1e2","title":"E